hi there Steve Kaufman again and next  I'm gonna change to these other glasses  that are less reflective um I want to  talk a little about the importance of  being an independent learner and and  this is one of the major attractions of  input based learning so I'm gonna stay  on this subject just did a video on on  what I consider to be the advantages of  listening and reading as opposed to  focusing on output and it has a lot to  do with the importance of being  independent because if you are worried  about your output at an early stage in  your language learning if you want to  practice output who are you gonna  practice with most people don't want to  talk to someone who can't speak very  well or who has very few words I don't  like it when someone comes to me and  says can I practice my English on you  and essentially can't say anything  I think it's an unreasonable expectation  of someone so you end up with a teacher  and again I think it's unnecessary to be  dependent on a teacher if you want to  practice your output on someone you have  you are dependent on their good will  that they are going to be patient and  they're gonna listen to you and try to  understand what you're saying and speak  slowly and and stay within the range of  the limited number of things that you  can talk about I prefer not to do that I  prefer to build myself up to a level  where I can have a conversation with  someone where I'm not a burden on them  and and you never know what their  reaction is going to be I mean some  people are patient some people are not  patient so learning by an input focusing  on listening and reading makes you more  independent and I think that is a major  major advantage I don't need to go to a  tutor I can if I want but I don't depend  on the two  and the other thing about a teaching  scenario is your traditional classroom  is one of dependence the learner is  dependent on the teacher and the teacher  decides what the activities are going to  be and I know from having been on this  list serve the community of English  teachers they spend a lot of time  talking to each other about how nice it  was that they introduced poetry or that  they brought up some subject in their  class on critical thinking which forced  the learners to question some aspect of  our society and forced them to be  critical thinkers but maybe those  learners were not interested in poetry  we're not interested in the subject that  you wanted them to become critical  thinkers of about mr. or mrs. teacher so  I think that the one of the major  disadvantages of a classroom is that the  learners are so dependent they just walk  in there and sit down and wait for the  teacher to take over the big advantage  of input but he's learning is that you  are in charge you decide what you're  gonna listen to you decide if you're  gonna spend the next hour listening or  reading or going through flashcards or  writing or if you choose to contact if  you do have a language exchange partner  you can also contact the language  exchange partner but once again once  you're depending on someone else's  goodwill you are no longer quite so  independent so I think a major major  advantage of input based learning is the  fact that you become independent and I  think that and I this is one of the  themes in my book it's so important to  cultivate that that capacity to be an  independent learner to explore the  language on your own I'm constantly  surprised at people who are as soon as  they run into the first difficulty in a  language they want it explained why is  this  on our forum now in Russian you know  yeah why are there not two dots over the  heat well it just isn't you'll get used  but a lot of things that people ask  questions about at an early stage  they eventually figure out themselves  and or again I find now that I've been  in Russia and I've been doing it for  four years now an hour a day mostly  listening and reading occasionally  reviewing a grammar book but I find it's  very useful now to go back to my  beginner books when I used to flip  through and ignore the grammar because I  couldn't remember it or make sense of it  and now I get walked through that book  it takes me probably you know between a  half an hour and an hour to go through  the whole book very quickly but I'd find  that I'm sort of confirming and nailing  down all of these rules that were  meaningless blurs to me before because  my emphasis has been building up my  vocabulary through all my listening and  reading activities and and being willing  to live with a certain amount of  uncertainty and and lack of clarity and  in the text and so now as an independent  learner I choose now to go back there  and try and nail down some of the  grammar some of the grammar has already  become second nature to me but I do  often often pick up some other things so  I just want to make this point that one  of the major advantages of what appears  to be a passive way of learning is that  you become independent you're not forced  to sit in the classroom where the  teachers gonna have you role-playing and  so or you know I had this great debate  with the Canadian Canadian benchmarks  system which is this thing that has been  developed in Canada over ten years and  up teen committee meetings and people  travelling around the countryside and  and they insist that any immigrant who  is learning English is obliged to learn  as long as the government's paying for  it using a system called task based  learning which means that the learner  sits in the classroom and pretends to be  a nurse or a checkout person in a suit  market or whatever other tasks they  decide the teacher decides or they might  say okay what do you diet would you know  ask the class work do they want to you  know what kind of a task that they want  to act out but the point is that the  decision on what to do in the classroom  is with the teacher and so the big  advantage of input based learning is  that you decide what the learning task  what the learning subject matter is  going to be and that is a big advantage  because if you can develop that ability  to be an independent learner you will  succeed more quickly than if you remain  in the position of a dependent learner  thank you for listening
 

